WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.533
A chain, each node delay 1, crossing clusters adds D = 3. Two clusters: one crossing, delay 7.

2
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.889
Another split crosses twice: delay 10.

3
00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:21.133
The goal has changed: the longest path's delay, not the cut.

4
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:26.733
The RW model: a combinational circuit is a directed acyclic graph.

5
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:29.533
Each node has a delay δ.

6
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:35.200
Wires inside a cluster add nothing; wires between clusters add a fixed D.

7
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.000
Each cluster has a capacity M.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.200
And nodes may be replicated: the premise of the optimality result.

9
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:51.733
The candidate DAG, reconstructed from the original film: 12 nodes, PIs a, b, c, POs k, l.

10
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:58.756
Δ(b, k) = 4: along b, e, g, i, k, counting the end, not the start.

11
00:00:58.756 --> 00:01:02.889
A PI's label is its own delay: 1.

12
00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:06.978
Label in topological order. Take node i.

13
00:01:06.978 --> 00:01:12.222
Each ancestor's score: l(x) + Δ(x, i).

14
00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:20.356
Capacity 4: take the top scores g, e, c; ties go to the later node in topological order, an assumption.

15
00:01:20.356 --> 00:01:27.156
PI c inside gives l1 = 4; b, the largest outside, gives l2 = 4 + 3 = 7.

16
00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:30.844
l(i) = 7. The label is a time.

17
00:01:31.244 --> 00:01:36.444
Recover from the outputs: first the candidate clusters of k and l.

18
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:41.467
The outside inputs d, e, f, h become new roots.

19
00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:46.489
b and c form their own: 8 clusters, 20 instances.

20
00:01:46.489 --> 00:01:51.067
Both outputs arrive at 8, exactly the labels.

21
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.600
Four things to keep.

22
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.667
Delay follows the longest path; labels are times;

23
00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:04.000
recover from the outputs, instances apart from logic nodes; replication costs area.

24
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.400
In the lab below, step through labelling and recovery.
